                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The core surface ship gameplay is generally great and there's no other game like it.\n\nUnfortunately, aircraft carriers (and hybrids, and to a lesser extent submarines) break the game and make it hard to enjoy at higher tier - especially on Asia server, where CVs played by Chinese sweatlords (who treat the game like Gaokao and prioritise winning at all costs over fun) are almost guaranteed in every battle, and you're entirely at their mercy with zero opportunity for counterplay. When the enemy CV decides your game is over, it's usually over. \n\nWargaming has recently doubled down on CV's god-like supremacy by deleting DFAA (the primary anti-air consumable), so you can't even cope into semi-defending yourself by playing a supposed \"anti-aircraft\" ship anymore.\n\nAdd to that the continual addition of silly overpowered gimmick ships which delete destroyers in a few seconds, and it's hard to recommend this game to anyone who wants fun strategic gameplay rather than frustration. WG took great core gameplay and have largely ruined it. Maybe they can bring it back in 2027 since they seem to realise the playerbase hates the latest anti-air changes, but I doubt it.\n\nWhat WG needs to change to fix this game:\n\n1.) Globally nerf all CV plane regeneration and damage-dealing (especially Essex, and including Hildebrand which is essentially a CV and played as such)\n2.) Bring back DFAA\n3.) Slow down with introducing new tier 10 ships, and stop with the perpetual gimmicks and powercreep e.g. Fuyutsuki, 20 de Julio, Taejong etc\n4.) Build more tutorial content into the game and nudge new (as well as experienced but bad) players into at least learning the basics of gameplay",
